<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gyaman</h1><p class="st-meta">1690 CE – 1895 CE (approx.) · capital Bondoukou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Abron kingdom around the Muslim trading town of Bondoukou, long a reluctant tributary of the Ashanti Empire on the border of modern Ghana and Ivory Coast.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gyaman was founded in the late 17th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bono-people">Abron</a> (Bono) migrants under their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tan-date">Tan Date</a>, who moved west from the Bono area to escape the rising power of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>. They settled around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bondoukou">Bondoukou</a>, an old town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wangara">Dyula</a> Muslim traders on the route between the goldfields and the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, and ruled the local peoples.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bono-people">Abron</a> kings, chosen from a royal matrilineage on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> model, held court at sites near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bondoukou">Bondoukou</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wangara">Dyula</a> scholars and merchants ran the trade in gold, kola and cloth. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> armies conquered Gyaman around 1740 and imposed tribute. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kofi-adinkra">Kofi Adinkra</a> revolted and was killed in 1818; Akan tradition links the adinkra cloth symbols to his name.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Gyaman regained autonomy after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> defeats in the 1870s, but in the 1890s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> divided it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samori-ture">Samori Toure</a> occupied it in 1895-1897. Its western part went to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-ivory-coast">French Ivory Coast</a> and the east to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gold-coast-colony">Gold Coast</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1690 CE – 1895 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.33%;width:4.08%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1690 CE – 1895 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bondoukou</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tan Date, Kofi Adinkra</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Akan traditional religion, Sunni Islam among traders</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Abron (Akan), Dyula</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a>, <a href="/countries/ghana">Ghana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gyaman, Abron kingdom, Bondoukou kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1792&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gyaman" aria-label="Kingdom of Gyaman on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4603 1877 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gyaman lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4923 2133L4973 2230M4923 2133L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4973 2230h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4923 2133h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4923 2133h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bondoukou. <a href="/atlas?year=1792&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gyaman">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

